d":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie","html_url":"https://github.com/GreenBudgie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GreenBudgie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T18:07:47Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T18:07:47Z","body":"I will just leave this comment here if anyone still struggles with this issue (still present in 4.5). The solution to disable physics interpolation for the `RigidBody2D` is not ideal, so I found a better way.\n\nHere is my solution keeps `RigidBody2D` interpolated while removing jittering from `GpuParticles2D`:\n1. Reparent `GpuParticles2D` node to another node higher in hierarchy (for example, to the root)\n2. Disable physics interpolation for `GpuParticles2D ` only (no need to disable interpolation for `RigidBody2D`!)\n3. Attach a script to `GpuParticles2D` and provide a reference to your `RigidBody2D`\n4. In `_process`, set the `GpuParticles2D` global position to `RigidBody2D`'s global position","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308888355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]